## Our sources

We base our guides on official and trusted sources. These include:

- **GOV.UK**, for benefit rules, rates and how to claim
- **legislation.gov.uk**, for the law itself, such as the PIP Regulations 2013
- **DWP guidance and statistics**
- **the NHS** and **NICE** (the National Institute for Health and Care Excellence), for health information
- **Upper Tribunal decisions**, which explain how benefit law should be applied
- **well-known charities**, such as Citizens Advice, Age UK, Versus Arthritis and Contact

Every guide lists the main sources we used at the bottom of the page.

## How we write

- We write in **plain English**, for a reading age of around 9 to 11, like GOV.UK and the NHS.
- We explain any word that may be unfamiliar.
- We tell you what the rules actually say, including when something may be difficult.
- We never promise that you will get a benefit.

## How we review

- Each guide shows the date it was **last checked** for accuracy.
- We check every guide **at least once a year**.
- We update **benefit rates every April**, when they change.
- We update guides as soon as we can when laws or official guidance change.

## Health information

Our health guides are based on NHS and NICE information. They are written to help you understand a condition and your options, not to replace advice from your own doctor.

At the moment our health guides are **not reviewed by a medical professional**. We plan to add clinical review in future, and we will show the reviewer's name and qualifications on each page when we do.

## How we use AI tools

We sometimes use AI tools to help with research, first drafts and checking. **A person always checks every page** against our sources before it is published, and is responsible for what it says. We do not publish anything written by AI without human review.

## Independence

- We are **not part of the DWP**, the NHS or any government body.
- Nobody can pay us to change what we write.
- Affiliate links never affect our advice. They are always clearly labelled. Read [how we make money](/affiliate-disclosure/).

## Corrections

If you think something on our website is wrong, please tell us at hello@juniperhealth.info. We will look into it quickly. If we made a mistake, we will fix it and update the "last checked" date on the page. If the mistake was important, we will add a short note to the page to say what changed.
